<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuan Shu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 199</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuan Shu was a Chinese warlord of the late Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> and cousin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shao">Yuan Shao</a>. Holding the Huainan region, he proclaimed himself emperor of a state called Zhong in 197, which made him an outcast among the other warlords. Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lu-bu">Lü Bu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a>, he tried to join Yuan Shao in the north in 199 but was blocked and died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuan-shu.jpg" alt="Yuan Shu" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yuan_Shu_Qing_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
